<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:wp81="using:Cornflower.Themes.Wp81">
  <!--
    The phone's HeaderContentPresenterStyle, the style every 8.1 template with a Header sets on its header's
    ContentPresenter (the Slider's, the TextBox's, the PasswordBox's, the ToggleSwitch's), as a keyed ControlTheme for
    ContentPresenter. A template sets it on its header part:

      <ContentPresenter x:Name="HeaderContentPresenter" Theme="{DynamicResource Wp81HeaderContentPresenterTheme}" />

    By DynamicResource: a StaticResource can't reach into another file (a control's theme is a file of its own).

    Its four values, and the phone's 1.33 em line for the text Avalonia's presenter makes of data (PhoneHeaderLine): a
    WinRT header doesn't recognise access keys, and nor does this one. What shows (Content, ContentTemplate) and where
    (Margin, IsVisible) are each template's own.

    The part's own theme ranks below its templated parent's theme, at style priority, so a template's /template/ style
    for the part wins over a value here: the ToggleSwitch's own brush, and each state's (the TextBox's :disabled
    header), as the phone's template's own Foreground and its states win over the style's.
  -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="Wp81HeaderContentPresenterTheme" TargetType="ContentPresenter">
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource PhoneFontFamilyNormal}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource TextStyleMediumFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource PhoneMidBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="wp81:PhoneHeaderLine.IsEnabled" Value="True" />
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
